          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, beginning at age 29. The epilepsy has an immune etiology associated with CASPR2 antibodies. Seizures are drug responsive on carbamazepine.\n\nCurrent Medication:\n- Carbamazepine, current antiseizure medication.\n\nSeizure Burden:\nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occur approximately twice per year.\n\nAssessment:\nGeneralized, drug-responsive epilepsy characterized by generalized tonic-clonic seizures, with CASPR2 antibody-associated immune etiology.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue carbamazepine.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,\nEpilepsy Clinic",
